context:
GET /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/discovery/operations/{discovery_id}
Returns a discovered web or API operation by discovery ID.
Required: zone_id (path); discovery_id (path) — Discovery ID of a discovered operation

PATCH /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/discovery/operations/{discovery_id}
Updates the state of a discovered web or API operation.
Required: zone_id (path); discovery_id (path) — Discovery ID of a discovered operation; body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/labels/user/{name}
Deletes a user-defined label and removes its associations with web and API operations.
Required: zone_id (path); name (path) — The label name

DELETE /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/operations/{operation_id}
Deletes a web or API operation from endpoint management so its feature configuration is no longer tracked.
Required: zone_id (path); operation_id (path) — Identifier for the operation

PATCH /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/labels/user/{name}
Updates only the supplied fields on a user-defined label.
Required: zone_id (path); name (path) — The label name; body (body)

PUT /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/labels/user/{name}
Replaces all editable fields on a user-defined label.
Required: zone_id (path); name (path) — The label name; body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/user_schemas/{schema_id}
Permanently removes an uploaded OpenAPI schema from API Shield schema validation. Operations using this schema will lose their validation rules. Deprecated; use `/zones/{zone_id}/schema_validation/schemas/{schema_id}` instead.
Required: zone_id (path); schema_id (path) — Identifier for the schema-ID

PATCH /client/v4/zones/{zone_id}/api_gateway/user_schemas/{schema_id}
Activates schema validation for an uploaded OpenAPI schema. Requests to matching endpoints will be validated against the schema definitions. Deprecated; use `/zones/{zone_id}/schema_validation/schemas/{schema_id}` instead.
Required: zone_id (path); schema_id (path) — Identifier for the schema-ID; body (body)
